# @@GOAL@@

Use the robot to @@GOAL@@. @@TASK_NOTES@@

You have **@@INTERACTION_STEPS@@ control steps** in one attempt. Observe and
experiment until satisfied, then call `finish()`. Exhausting the budget or
ending your turn also submits the current scene. Every control step counts;
`reset()` restores the same initial scene, discards progress, and costs one step.
Reconnecting preserves the attempt.

```python
from harness.client import TabletopClient
from PIL import Image

sim = TabletopClient()
obs = sim.observe()
Image.fromarray(obs["images"]["left"]).save("/workspace/left.png")
# Interact, then submit the current scene:
# sim.finish()
```

API and robot control documentation is in `/opt/rlebench/harness/client.py`,
also available through Python `help()`. Observations provide RGB images and
robot proprioception. Infer object locations and physical properties by
observing and interacting with the scene.
